            "date": "2020-11-04T20:38:22Z"
          },
          "message": "Get Docker builds working (#815)\n\n* chore(Docker): Update Java version in Dockerfile\n\nSort of fixes #794\nAnd applies the suggestion from https://github.com/spinnaker/kayenta/issues/794#issuecomment-698872876\nLike the subsequent comment notes, the build still fails when gradle hits the integration tests. I assume commenting it out isn't an option so going with just these changes for now.\n\n* chore(Docker): Don't run tests when building in Docker\n\nSince the integration tests try to spin up a Docker container, doing so\nwithin a Docker build would be weird. I'm sure there's some way to do\nit, but I'm not sure how and I'm not sure if it's a good idea. Since\ninteg tests run in CI, it seems OK to remove them from the Docker build.\n\nCo-authored-by: Justin Field <justin.field@armory.io>",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "114bf899520aa440e93050ca59acd0b92b456570",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/kayenta/git/trees/114bf899520aa440e93050ca59acd0b92b456570"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/kayenta/git/commits/90f5b105e285f147cc4a069f62def9e1a9132440",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJfoxE+CRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAdHIIACkwBkzD10quzx0oFa2OZ5YI\nUYjXv3aG+pmy0ZWIE/2+b+SRDIggl0pmeWmPK8dSO+9x3463eltiQIMFewiNRBHA\n1Tp46wnIFtjluyA3Rzg/+v5M82UhshLkUMBvilz4XTVAaKraKx84OtIF2Sdb6lto\nSEtN2/bR14wXalziBEGwkqvijxGhjp0/KRjG6nQdxmHtmtQCpgrzMrWlpviuGPKM\nrK2buqi0xQjvFA0xTnoq6bIQXoT1+fYybDfLsLTTl+h89zWE9wK29lCrsWayP4li\n4752Y7j7Uvy2ad+N2NmSuIntD3Y0kgfSxfyQ6oE9LydK4VfTiSUrmn6OnuiX8WM=\n=FbC6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree 114bf899520aa440e93050ca59acd0b92b456570\nparent 30ed2aabe80bb93d429505812d177ea6936dd927\nauthor Sam Park <spark.did.a.code@gmail.com> 1604522302 -0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1604522302 +0000\n\nGet Docker builds working (#815)\n\n* chore(Docker): Update Java version in Dockerfile\n\nSort of fixes #794\nAnd applies the suggestion from https://github.com/spinnaker/kayenta/issues/794#issuecomment-698872876\nLike the subsequent comment notes, the build still fails when gradle hits the integration tests. I assume commenting it out isn't an option so going with just these changes for now.\n\n* chore(Docker): Don't run tests when building in Docker\n\nSince the integration tests try to spin up a Docker container, doing so\nwithin a Docker build would be weird. I'm sure there's some way to do\nit, but I'm not sure how and I'm not sure if it's a good idea. Since\ninteg tests run in CI, it seems OK to remove them from the Docker build.\n\nCo-authored-by: Justin Field <justin.field@armory.io>"
          }
